{{also|blood bath}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|blood bath}}

===Etymology===
Coined in [[w:1867|1867]]. Compound of {{af|en|blood|bath}}, the latter used referring to a metaphorical [[deluge]]. Compare {{cog|fy|bloedbad|t=bloodbath}}, {{cog|nl|bloedbad|t=bloodbath}}, {{cog|de|Blutbad|t=bloodbath}}, {{cog|da|blodbad|t=bloodbath}}, {{cog|sv|blodbad|t=bloodbath}}, {{cog|is|blóðbad|t=bloodbath}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈblʌdˌbæθ/}}

